  "screenwriter_raw": "{\n  \"pseudos\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p1\",\n      \"text\": \"In the regulatory arena where the battle for digital fairness is being fought, European authorities have stood firm against a dominant gatekeeper. After years of investigation into how the tech giant ranks its own shopping, flight, and hotel services above competitors in search results, the guardians of fair competition refused to accept the corporation's weak concessions. They are now finalizing a decisive financial blow—a substantial antitrust fine that will add to more than a decade of competition enforcement actions against Alphabet.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.85,\n      \"center\": \"who-0\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"focal\": true,\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\n          \"why-0\",\n          \"how-0\",\n          \"how-1\",\n          \"how-2\",\n          \"result-0\",\n          \"result-1\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p2\",\n      \"text\": \"Brussels has rejected the company's remedy proposals after a long and determined investigation into unfair self-preferencing in search rankings. European regulators—the enforcers upholding EU regulations—are preparing a decisive financial blow against the multinational corporation for rigging search results to favor its own services. The monetary sanction, expected to reach the high hundreds of millions of euros, marks the latest chapter in a protracted fight to hold the powerful to account before the Commission's August recess.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.8,\n      \"center\": \"how-1\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"focal\": false,\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\n          \"why-0\",\n          \"how-0\",\n          \"how-1\",\n          \"how-2\",\n          \"result-0\",\n          \"result-1\",\n          \"how-3\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p3\",\n      \"text\": \"For years, the search engine provider favored its own comparison 